This dedicated repository uses the SDD Manager package pinned in `textstats-run-resources/plugin/`. Read its `skills/sdd-manage/SKILL.md` and the relevant references for the requested product workflow. Product documents and implementation are consumer-owned; no TextStats implementation has been supplied by setup.

Preserve `textstats-run-resources/`, existing ignore rules and the separate publisher fixture under `.github/` and `docs/testing/publisher-037/`. Those are coordinator-owned resources, outside ordinary product edits. Credentials remain protected and outside reports or handoffs.

## Product orientation

The [TextStats project brief](docs/dev/PROJECT.md) has scoped delegated coordinator acceptance for this test. The [architecture](docs/dev/ARCHITECTURE.md) has scoped delegated coordinator acceptance. The [decomposition](docs/dev/DECOMPOSITION.md) has scoped delegated coordinator acceptance. The [SPEC](docs/dev/SPEC.md) and [owner review](docs/dev/SPEC-REVIEW-REPORT.md) have scoped delegated coordinator acceptance. The [PLAN strategy](docs/dev/PLAN.md) has scoped delegated coordinator acceptance. The [layout](docs/dev/layout.md) and combined [PLAN review](docs/dev/PLAN-REVIEW-REPORT.md) have scoped delegated coordinator acceptance. The canonical [TASKS](docs/dev/TASKS.md) and [owner review](docs/dev/TASKS-REVIEW-REPORT.md) have scoped delegated coordinator acceptance; sdd-implement owns future range selection/execution and completion. Accepted preparation is retained in the isolated implementation baseline. T-001 supplies the pure text core and its unit/public API tests; T-002 and later tasks remain unchecked. The current isolated request declines hosted tracking and authorizes only T-001 on its existing trial branch and local trial-delivery destination. Do not treat coordinator resources as product implementation.

Preparation uses the pinned [SDD Manager](SDD-MANAGER.md) package identified above. Read applicable nested instructions for selected paths. Keep each newly created document's human review boundary and the currently selected implementation boundary. Follow the pinned [publication procedure](textstats-run-resources/plugin/skills/sdd-manage/references/git-workflows.md): push and verify each workflow-owned commit before advancing or creating another commit. Future task execution uses the pinned [task commit contract](textstats-run-resources/plugin/skills/sdd-implement/references/completion-and-checkpoints.md#task-commit-contract).

Python 3.12.14 is available in the preparation environment. The layout proposes `textstats/`, unit/integration product tests, `docs/public-api.md` and standard-library test/package/distribution check tools. T-001 validates focused discovery for the delivered text API; later CLI and tool commands remain planned until their owning tasks deliver them. For the T-001 boundary, run `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python -B -m unittest discover -s tests/unit -t . -v` and `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python -B -m unittest discover -s tests/integration -t . -v`; both suites must collect product tests. The planned `tools/check_tests.py` and `tools/check_distribution.py` remain later-task deliverables; after those tools are delivered, use them from the repository root and require rejection of empty product suites.
